{"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection","title":"Cliques","externalID":"Cliques","modules":[{"name":"Cliques"}],"symbolKind":"module"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/cliques"]}],"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/AllCliques","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/BronKerboschEvents","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/ClusteringCoefficients","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/CoreNumbers","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/OnionLayers","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/TreeDecomposition","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/TrussNumbers"],"title":"Structures","anchor":"Structures"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/BronKerboschEvent"],"title":"Enumerations","anchor":"Enumerations"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols"],"title":"Extended Modules","anchor":"Extended-Modules"}],"references":{"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/MaximalCliques":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every maximal clique of an undirected graph’s simple graph once, lazily, each in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order (by vertex index): an isolated vertex, or one whose only edges are loops, is a clique of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one. The order is Eppstein–Löffler–Strash’s: by the cliques’ first vertex in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"coreNumbers().degeneracyOrdering"},{"type":"text","text":", then as Bron–Kerbosch with Tomita’s pivot (ties to the least"},{"type":