ype":"text"},{"text":"each in ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order (by vertex index). The order is by the cliques’ first vertex in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"coreNumbers().degeneracyOrdering","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", then depth first, each clique followed by its extensions by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"later vertices in ascending index. The sequence holds the graph, so iterating again gives the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same cliques. O(n + m) before the first clique, O(d) bitset words per clique for degeneracy d."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/AllCliques","title":"AllCliques"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/BronKerboschEvents":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/bronkerboschevents","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"BronKerboschEvents"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"BronKerboschEvents"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The Bron–Kerbosch algorithm with pivoting as a sequence of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BronKerboschEvent"},{"text":"s: the search of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maximalCliques()"},{"text":", one clique at a time. Pulling an event past the last one kept runs the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"search to its next maximal clique and keeps the events on the way.","type":"text"}],"title":"BronKerboschEvents","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/BronKerboschEvents"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/OnionLayers":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The onion decomposition of an undirected graph’s simple graph: each vertex’s layer, a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"refinement of the core decomposition in which every layer lies inside one k-shell. Layers are"},{